<div id="recipe-89732-ingredients" class="wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-ingredients-no-images wprm-recipe-89732-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before" data-recipe="89732" data-servings="1"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Ingredients</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="0"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">butternut squash</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">3 lbs</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="1"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">of olive oil</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="2"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">kosher salt</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="3"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">black pepper</span></li></ul></div></div>
<div id="recipe-89732-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-89732-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="89732"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-89732-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Preheat oven to 375&deg;F (190&deg;C). There is no need to line the sheet pan with parchment paper.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-89732-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place the whole butternut squash on its side on your cutting board. Hold it firmly in the middle with your non-dominant hand. Trim the stem (the top) by cutting about &frac12;-inch off.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-89732-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">While still holding it firmly on its side, cut it vertically (or from top to bottom direction) in the middle. I recommend cutting one side first and then turning it around and cutting the other side next. As you are cutting you may have to jerk it back and forth while applying a little pressure to loosen it. Remove the seeds with a spoon and discard them.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-89732-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Place the halved butternut squash cut side up on a baking sheet. Brush the cut side with olive oil and sprinkle it with salt and pepper.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-89732-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Roast in the oven for about 50-55 minutes or until it turns golden brown. The timing might be a bit more or less depending on the size of your butternut squash. You can also check doneness by inserting a knife in "the neck" (the narrow upper part) of the squash. If it comes in and out easily it should be ready to go.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-89732-step-0-5" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Let it cool for 5 minutes, use it in your recipe right away or scoop the flesh to use it later.</div></li></ul></div></div>
