<div id="recipe-89732-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><span style="display: block;"><strong>Make-ahead and storage: </strong><span style="font-weight: 400;">You can roast butternut squash halves up to 3 days before you plan to use them.&nbsp;</span></span><div class="wprm-spacer"></div>
<span style="display: block;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">To store, let them cool to room temperature, then wrap them in </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">plastic wrap (or store them in an airtight container) and refrigerate for up to 3 days.</span></span><div class="wprm-spacer"></div>
<span style="display: block;">To reheat, place them on a sheet pan, cut-side up, and warm in a preheated 350&deg;F oven for 10 to 15 minutes, until thoroughly heated through.</span></div></div>
